              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+formation"} introduce it as a type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term+introduction"} introduce terms
            of that type, how to use or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term+elimination"} eliminate terms
            of that type, and how to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rule"} compute
            when we combine the constructors with the eliminators.
          %p
            The unit type, like the binary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+type"} product type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+type"} positive type
            and as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+type"} negative type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lambda-calculus"} lambda-calculus
          %h3#in_natural_deduction In natural deduction
          %p
            We assume that our unit types have typal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conversion+rules"} conversion rules
          %p For both the positive unit type and the negative unit type, the formation and introduction rules are the same.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formation+rule"} formation rule
            for the unit type is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathbb{1} \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/introduction+rule"} introduction rule
            for the unit type is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash *:\mathbb{1}}
          %p
            The positive unit type says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
            satisfies
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+induction"} singleton induction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *:\mathbb{1}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center+of+contraction"} center of contraction
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
          %h4#as_a_positive_type As a positive type
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+induction"} Singleton induction
            for a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
            and term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *:\mathbb{1}
            states that the type has the following
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elimination+rule"} elimination rule
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rule"} computation rule
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+rule"} uniqueness rule
          %ul
            %li
              given a type family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x)
              indexed by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟙
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:\mathbb{1}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:C(*)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ind
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{ind}_\mathbb{1}^C(x, c):C(x)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ind
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{1} \vdash C(x) \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{1}, c:C(*) \vdash \mathrm{ind}_\mathbb{1}^C(x, c):C(x)}
          %ul
            %li
              given a type family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x)
              indexed by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟙
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:C(*)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ind
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{ind}_\mathbb{1}^C(*, c)
              derived from the elimination rule is equal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              with witness
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi β
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_\mathbb{1}^C(c)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msubsup
                        %mi β
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ind
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{1} \vdash C(x) \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, c_*:C(*) \vdash \beta_\mathbb{1}^C(c):\mathrm{ind}_\mathbb{1}^C(*, c) =_{C(*)} c}
          %ul
            %li
              given a type family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x)
              indexed by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
              and a family of elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u(x):C(x)
              indexed by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟙
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:\mathbb{1}
              there is a witness
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_\mathbb{1}^C(x, u(x))
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u(x)
              is equal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ind
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{ind}_\mathbb{1}^{C}(x, u(*))
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msubsup
                        %mi η
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ind
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{1} \vdash C(x) \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma, x:\mathbb{1} \vdash u(x):C(x)}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{1} \vdash \eta_\mathbb{1}^C(x, u(x)):u(x) =_{C(x)} \mathrm{ind}_\mathbb{1}^{C}(x, u(*))}
          %p
            Thus, the unit type satisfies
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+induction"} singleton induction
          %p In type theories with a separate type judgment where not all types are elements of universes, one has to additionally add the following elimination and computation rules:
          %p Elimination rules:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} typerec
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{1} \vdash \mathrm{typerec}_{\mathbb{1}}^{A}(x) \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p Computation rules:
          %ul
            %li judgmental computation rules
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} typerec
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{typerec}_{\mathbb{1}}^{A}(*) \equiv A \; \mathrm{type}}
          %ul
            %li
              typal computation rules
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %msubsup
                            %mi β
                            %mi 𝟙
                            %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %msubsup
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} typerec
                            %mi 𝟙
                            %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \beta_{\mathbb{1}}^{A}:\mathrm{typerec}_{\mathbb{1}}^{A}(*) \simeq A}
          %h4#as_a_negative_type As a negative type
          %p
            As a negative type, there are no
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elimination+rules"} elimination rules
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rules"} computation rules
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+rule"} uniqueness rule
            states that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center+of+contraction"} center of contraction
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
            and is given by:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi 𝟙
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi 𝟙
                      %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma, p:\mathbb{1} \vdash \eta_\mathbb{1}(p):* =_\mathbb{1} p}
          %p
            Thus, the unit type is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible type
          %h4#positive_versus_negative Positive versus negative
          %p
          .num_theorem
